Falsifies `filesystem_proto::dir::Rights::a_root_carries_nothing_undefined`.

The defect: the mask dropped from `Rights::root`, `Rights(mask)` instead of
`Rights(mask & ALL)`. The caller of `root` is holding a mask that came off the wire, so
this is the same shape as `capability`'s `from_bits` hole one protocol along: an
undefined bit smuggled in today acquires a meaning the day somebody defines that bit.

Expected to fail: `assert!(Rights::root(mask).bits() & !ALL == 0)`, on any mask with an
undefined bit set.

diff --git a/crates/filesystem_proto/src/lib.rs b/crates/filesystem_proto/src/lib.rs
index a52f1ef1..02a62d47 100644
--- a/crates/filesystem_proto/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/filesystem_proto/src/lib.rs
@@ -1042,7 +1042,7 @@ pub mod dir {
         /// The rights the endpoint's bound directory carries. This is the only place a rights set is
         /// made out of thin air, and the only caller is the code that binds a server to a directory.
         pub const fn root(mask: u64) -> Self {
-            Rights(mask & ALL)
+            Rights(mask)
         }
 
         /// **The child's rights: what the parent has, intersected with what was asked for.**
